### Bingux Files.
### Source language: British English. Conventions: docs/bingux-ui.md,
### "Localisation". Every ID starts with `files-`.
### Only the app's own strings are here. The menus and views of the file
### manager live in the `bingux-ui` catalogue (`ui-files-`).

# The app's name, in the window title, the header and the About window.
files-title = Files
# One line in the About window.
files-description = Browse and organise files and folders

## Closing a window while a file operation runs

# Title of the dialog that asks before a window closes during a file operation.
files-close-guard-title = Close Files?
# Message of the dialog that asks before a window closes during a file operation.
files-close-guard-message = A file operation is still running. Closing the window stops it.

## Window commands

# Command in the window's menu and the command palette: opens a new window.
files-command-new-window = New window
